## Why This Is Asked
Tests incident-response planning across Defender for Cloud, Azure AD, Key Vault, and cross-subscription governance.

## Key Concepts
- Automated incident response playbooks
- Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed identities and service principals
- Canary rollouts and rollback strategies
- Cross-subscription isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Rotate secret using Node.js Azure SDK
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const vault = new SecretClient(`https://${'ProdKV'}.vault.azure.net`, new DefaultAzureCredential());
async function rotate(){ const newVal = require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64');
  await vault.setSecret('dbPassword', newVal);
}
rotate().catch(console.error);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CMK usage, Key Vault integration, identity access, policy enforcement, and rollback planning at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage at rest
- Azure Key Vault with managed identities
- Storage Account encryption properties and keyVaultProperties
- Azure Policy to require CMK on new storage accounts
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// ARM-like snippet illustrating CMK encryption on a storage account
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
  "name": "[storageAccountName]",
  "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "properties": {
    "encryption": {
      "keySource": "Microsoft.KeyVault",
      "keyVaultProperties": {
        "keyName": "<cmk-name>",
        "keyVaultUri": "https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

