## Why This Is Asked

This question probes real-world guardrail design for ML deployments in a multi-tenant Azure environment, focusing on data isolation, secret management, and trustworthy rollout processes.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Lighthouse and cross-tenant delegation
- Row-Level Security and Dynamic Data Masking
- Canary deployments and automatic rollback
- Azure Policy to enforce Key Vault references
- Data provenance and model-output leakage mitigation
- UEBA monitoring and cross-tenant audit trails

## Code Example

```json
{
  \"policyRule\": {
    \"if\": {
      \"anyOf\": [
        {\"field\": \"type\", \"equals\": \"Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets\"},
        {\"field\": \"siteConfig.appSettings[0]\", \"exists\": true}
      ]
    },
    \"then\": {\"effect\": \"deny\"}
  }
}
```

